  "title": "US Justice Department Investigates TV Networks Over Trump Pool Coverage",
  "summary": "The US Department of Justice is investigating whether the White House television press pool's decision to block coverage of President Donald Trump's activities violated antitrust law, following a ban on major news outlets like CNN, MS NOW, and Politico. The White House press pool, a rotating cast of news outlets, has become a proxy for the broader fight over whether the president or anyone can control the content of news reports.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The US Department of Justice is investigating whether the decision of the White House television press pool to halt coverage of President Donald Trump last month violated antitrust law.",
      "confidence": 0.95
